    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Triage inbound emails with AI and draft replies for review\n\nEvery new email gets read, classified and answered with a draft, while a human keeps the final say. Built for founders, agencies and support teams whose inbox is the front door of the business.\n\n### How it works\n1. The Gmail trigger picks up each new email and a code step normalizes sender, subject and body.\n2. Claude returns a structured verdict: category (sales, support, billing, spam, other), priority, sentiment, detected language, a one-line summary, a draft reply and a needs-human-review flag.\n3. A guardrail coerces the model output to allowed values and flags anything malformed, so raw model text is never trusted.\n4. Spam is logged and stopped. Everything else becomes a ready-to-review Gmail draft, never auto-sent, plus a row in Google Sheets.\n5. High-priority or sales mail also fires a Slack alert.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add a Gmail OAuth2 credential on the Gmail Trigger and Create draft reply nodes.\n2. Add an Anthropic credential on the Chat model node, or swap in any chat model n8n supports.\n3. Add a Google Sheets credential on the two Log nodes, and set the environment variable TRIAGE_SHEET_ID to a spreadsheet that contains a tab named email_triage.\n4. Optional: add a Slack credential and set the target channel on Slack alert.\n\n### Customization tips\nEdit the attributes and the system prompt in AI: classify and draft to match your business. Allowed categories and priorities live in one place inside the Validate node. Swap Slack for Telegram, or Gmail for Outlook, without touching the AI logic.",
        "width": 660,
        "height": 1000
      },
